{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_packing_data_research_document", "label": "Packing weight and volume research", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/PACKING_DATA_RESEARCH.md", "source_location": "L1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_packing_data_research_template_specific_quantity_semantics", "label": "Template-specific quantity semantics", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/PACKING_DATA_RESEARCH.md", "source_location": "L32", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "This interpretation must be attached to the source template or explicit unit, not inferred from a destination country. Other observed conventions include: - LY THANH: `PACK=100Gr.`, `QUANTITY=5`, `UNIT=KGS.` gives 50 packs and 5 kg."}, {"id": "docs_packing_data_research_exact_kilogram_to_pack_conversion", "label": "Exact kilogram-to-pack conversion", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/PACKING_DATA_RESEARCH.md", "source_location": "L30", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "`pack count = ordered kg \u00d7 1000 / pack grams`. This interpretation must be attached to the source template or explicit unit, not inferred from a destination country. Other observed conventions include:"}, {"id": "docs_packing_data_research_fractional_pack_review", "label": "Fractional pack review", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/PACKING_DATA_RESEARCH.md", "source_location": "L86", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Do not silently floor or ceil a fractional pack count. Either correct the order, confirm a partial-pack policy, or retain a separate loose-weight line with its own packing treatment. Cross-check explicit line net weight against pack count times nominal weight. Surface differences instead of overwriting either source value."}, {"id": "docs_packing_data_research_finished_pack_occupied_volume", "label": "Finished-pack occupied volume", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/PACKING_DATA_RESEARCH.md", "source_location": "L97", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Occupied space of the finished pack is the quantity the box planner needs. It includes the effects of the bag or tray, shape, stems and gaps. It does not require dimensions for every individual vegetable."}, {"id": "docs_packing_data_research_bulk_density_comparators", "label": "Bulk-density comparators", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/PACKING_DATA_RESEARCH.md", "source_location": "L103", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "`estimated produce bulk volume (cm3) = nominal pack grams / bulk density (g/cm3)`. Equivalently:"}, {"id": "docs_packing_data_research_evidence_before_profile_approval", "label": "Evidence before profile approval", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/PACKING_DATA_RESEARCH.md", "source_location": "L169", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "- Keep estimate provenance separate from approval. The existing reviewed-profile gate must not be bypassed by importing web estimates or generic family values. A future estimate-preview option can expose draft plans without approving them. - Product profile keys must include SKU, nominal size and bag/tray/bunch form."}, {"id": "docs_packing_data_research_finished_pack_sample_method", "label": "Finished-pack sample method", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/PACKING_DATA_RESEARCH.md", "source_location": "L139", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "### Practical measurement without individual produce dimensions Use several finished packs in their normal bag, tray or bunch form. Place them naturally in a container with known internal dimensions. Measure the area and"}, {"id": "docs_packing_data_research_fao_density_definitions", "label": "FAO density definitions", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/PACKING_DATA_RESEARCH.md", "source_location": "L112", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "material density does not describe the same occupied space. FAO distinguishes these concepts in its [density database, definitions on printed p5](https://www.fao.org/fileadmin/templates/food_composition/documents/density_DB_v2_0_01.pdf). Use the following preference order:"}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_packing_data_research_document", "target": "docs_packing_data_research_template_specific_quantity_semantics", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/PACKING_DATA_RESEARCH.md", "source_location": "L32", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_packing_data_research_document", "target": "docs_packing_data_research_exact_kilogram_to_pack_conversion", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/PACKING_DATA_RESEARCH.md", "source_location": "L30", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_packing_data_research_document", "target": "docs_packing_data_research_fractional_pack_review", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/PACKING_DATA_RESEARCH.md", "source_location": "L86", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_packing_data_research_document", "target": "docs_packing_data_research_finished_pack_occupied_volume", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/PACKING_DATA_RESEARCH.md", "source_location": "L97", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_packing_data_research_document", "target": "docs_packing_data_research_bulk_density_comparators", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/PACKING_DATA_RESEARCH.md", "sourc